===Talk to Natasha{{subst:void|<!--201140101-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|Natasha sends you a message. It seems that she wants to talk about some personal stuff with you.<br />Of course you won't refuse her invitation. Go meet her at the clinic when you have time.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
----
:'''Natasha:''' (Trailblazer), can I talk to you for a moment? I have a favor to ask. Something... rather personal.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Of course, Nat.
::'''Natasha:''' I want to thank you again for recovering the wonder medicine. It meant a lot to me.
::'''Natasha:''' But disposing of Vache's reagents isn't enough to solve the medical supply shortage. Many of my patients can't be seen promptly, and my stock of medicine is running low.
::'''Natasha:''' Thanks to you, the route to the Overworld through the Furnace Core has reopened. I'd like to use it to return to the surface and see if I can get some help.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Help from whom?
:::'''Natasha:''' I knew you'd be interested.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} If you need recovery meds, I've got some in my bag...
:::'''Natasha:''' Hehe, funny as always, (Trailblazer).
::'''Natasha:''' Remember my adoptive parents I mentioned to you a while ago?
::'''Natasha:''' After the reopening of the Furnace Core passage, I had an idea. I wrote a letter and asked Sampo to deliver it to my parents' old address.
::'''Natasha:''' I didn't have high hopes, but amazingly, Sampo brought me my mother's reply.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sampo being a gentleman... a rare occurrence...
:::'''Natasha:''' Hehe, that's exactly what I thought when I got her letter.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sampo couldn't have forged it, could he?
:::'''Natasha:''' No, I recognize my family's handwriting. We are all doctors after all.
::'''Natasha:''' Mom said they still live at the old house, but they're not working on the front lines anymore. They should still have some connections in the medical school and the hospital, though.
::'''Natasha:''' If I'm lucky, maybe I can convince them to send extra medical supplies to the Underworld.
::'''Natasha:''' Of course, that's not the only reason for me to go back to the surface... I can't wait to visit my parents again, and I can tell from my mom's letter that they feel the same.
::'''Natasha:''' If possible, I would like you to go with me, (Trailblazer).
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Of course.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I won't say no to you.
::'''Natasha:''' ...Wonderful, that's such a relief.
::'''Natasha:''' I've sent another letter to my mom telling her to find us near Fountain Plaza. Don't worry, I know my way around the Administrative District.
::----
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I have other things to attend to...
::'''Natasha:''' It's okay, I understand. You must have some important things on your plate? Don't let them get ahead of you.
::----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Meet Natasha in the Overworld{{subst:void|<!--201140102-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Administrative District|update|Natasha has reconnected with her adoptive parents living in the Overworld, hoping that their network in the medical community could help the patients in the Underworld obtain more medical resources.<br />Natasha wants you to come with her, because it has been more than ten years since the last time she stepped in the Administrative District.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
----
:'''Natasha:''' ...this place doesn't seem to have changed much from what I remember.
:'''Natasha:''' ...Oh, there you are. Sorry, I got distracted watching the crowds.
:'''Natasha:''' (Trailblazer), look at the busy flow of people &mdash; life in the Overworld carries on as usual, as if nothing has happened.
:'''Natasha:''' We're a little early. I've got an idea...
:'''Natasha:''' I want to buy my mom a gift. (Trailblazer), you're more of an Overworld local than I am now. Any suggestions?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How about flowers from Eversummer Florist?
::'''Natasha:''' Flowers, huh?
::'''Natasha:''' That's a great idea. I've been underground for so long, I almost forgot what flowers smell like.
::'''Natasha:''' Flowers it is then, (Trailblazer). Can you lead the way?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How about watching a play at Golden Theater?
::'''Natasha:''' A play... hmm...
::'''Natasha:''' Sounds fun, but there's a chance it won't suit my mom's taste. Let me think...
::'''Natasha:''' Oh, yes! I remember there was a florist in the Overworld. How about we head over that way?
::'''Natasha:''' I've been underground for so long, I already forgot what flowers smell like.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} To Neverwinter Workshop...
::'''Natasha:''' Workshop? I'm not too sure about that... Let's see if we have other options.
::'''Natasha:''' Oh, yes! I remember there was a florist in the Overworld. How about we head over that way?
::'''Natasha:''' I've been underground for so long, I already forgot what flowers smell like.
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Go to the Eversummer Florist{{subst:void|<!--201140103-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Eversummer Florist|update|Natasha has reconnected with her adoptive parents living in the Overworld, hoping that their network in the medical community could help the patients in the Underworld obtain more medical resources.<br />You meet Natasha in the Administrative District, but there is still some time left before meeting her adoptive mother.<br />Since they haven't met each other for a long time, Natasha decides to buy a flower bouquet as a gift for her adoptive parents.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
:'''Natasha:''' Eversummer... Was that always the name? Seems I was too young to get the irony back then.
:'''Natasha:''' ...Sorry, don't mean to sound cynical. Maybe it simply represents the people's hopes up here.
:'''Natasha:''' Now that I think about it, sending flowers is quite the tradition in my family. Mom, dad, Vache, and I... whenever something good happened, we sent each other flowers to celebrate.
:'''Natasha:''' Do you want to hear a flower story, (Trailblazer)?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Let's hear one, Nat.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What was your mother's favorite flower...?
:::'''Natasha:''' Each year for their anniversary, my dad would send my mom a bouquet of Ball Peonies wrapped in red paper.
:::'''Natasha:''' I heard that Ball Peonies represent "love that knows no end..." It does fit their marriage.
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What was your father's favorite flower...?
::::'''Natasha:''' My father is a famous surgeon in Belobog. Because of his fame, people in medical circles paid great attention to his surgeries... He always had a lot of stress to deal with.
::::'''Natasha:''' Each time he finished a tricky operation, my mom and I would buy a single stem of Sunshine, then pin it on the chest pocket of his apron.
::::'''Natasha:''' Sunshines represent "warmth and love of light..." For patients on the verge of death, my dad might have been the only light to penetrate the darkness around them.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What was Vache's favorite flower...?
::::'''Natasha:''' Vache... Out of everyone in my family, I think he probably appreciated flowers the least.
::::'''Natasha:''' Still, I remember the day he received his offer from the medical academy. My parents took me to the florist and we bought him the most expensive Marquise stem in the shop.
::::'''Natasha:''' When we gave him the flower, he failed to hide his smile. You can't imagine how hard it was to get him to smile.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What's your favorite flower...?
::::'''Natasha:''' As an orphan, I never knew my birthday. My adoptive parents took me to the Overworld and made the day I joined the family my birthday.
::::'''Natasha:''' Each year on that day, my parents would give me a bouquet of First Snow. The number of stems represented how many years had passed since I joined the family.
::::'''Natasha:''' I only found out later that First Snow represents "beautiful memories." My parents gave me a beautiful childhood, and I still haven't had the chance to thank them for that...
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I see. Shall we go to the florist?
