:'''Natasha:''' Mr. Oswell? I thought you headed back home with mom. How come...?
:'''Butler Oswell:''' I apologize, Miss Natasha! As a matter of fact... there's something I have to tell you in person.
:'''Natasha:''' Something that mom isn't supposed to know?
:'''Butler Oswell:''' You haven't changed a bit &mdash; smart and sensitive. The fact of the matter is... in the first two years after the passage was closed off, I received many letters from Master Vache.
:'''Natasha:''' ...What? Letters from Vache? Are you certain, Mr. Oswell?
:'''Butler Oswell:''' Of course, Miss. I recognized his handwriting. You'll see what I mean when you read the letters yourself.
:'''Butler Oswell:''' Actually... those letters were intended for your eyes only. The delivery address was the Underworld, but because of the sealing off of the passageway, the letters were sent back to your old house, to me.
:'''Natasha:''' I don't understand &mdash; did you not show them to my parents?
:'''Butler Oswell:''' I... I'm sorry, Miss. I opened one of them out of curiosity. Master Vache stressed in the letter that your parents must not know what happened to him...
:'''Butler Oswell:''' That's why I put the letters in a secure place, waiting to hand them to you when we could meet again.
:'''Natasha:''' ...
:'''Butler Oswell:''' I... I'm not sure if I did the right thing, Miss Natasha. I just didn't want your parents to feel that their son was so close and yet so far away...
:'''Natasha:''' ...Do you have the letters on you, Mr. Oswell? Let me take a look.
:'''Butler Oswell:''' Of course, of course &mdash; here... You can tell it's the young master's handwriting.
<pre>{
