:'''Natasha:''' ...
:'''Natasha:''' "The cold has revealed to me my arrogance. How can a child who grew up in warmth ever begin to comprehend a cure to bitter cold."
:'''Natasha:''' He... Vache didn't give up on his research into Blizzard Immunity... even after he left the city.
:'''Natasha:''' "I live in abandoned houses under broken roofs and continue my experiments. One step after another, I've made breakthroughs. I'm trembling, not because of the cold... but because I can feel I'm getting closer to the answer I seek..."
:'''Natasha:''' If what's in here is true, then Vache must have built a lab somewhere in the Snow Plains... and even made progress in his research. But how can that be...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do you believe it?
::'''Natasha:''' There'd be no point in him lying to me in the letters. Still, it's possible he may have gone completely insane before he started writing them...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Maybe he went mad...
::'''Natasha:''' It's possible. But what if he was still sane when he wrote this down...
:'''Natasha:''' (Trailblazer), I need to leave the city to recover my brother's research data. Are you willing to come with me?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sure thing.
::'''Butler Oswell:''' Leave the city? You are taking too much risk, Miss Natasha...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's dangerous outside the city walls...
::'''Butler Oswell:''' This {{MC|ж=young lady|м=young gentleman}} is right. Danger is everywhere beyond the walls of Belobog...
:<!--1-second delay-->
:'''Natasha:''' I know, Mr. Oswell. But I have a hero with me &mdash; {{MC|ж=she|м=he}} saved the Underworld. I'm sure {{MC|ж=she'll|м=he'll}} protect me, right?
:'''Natasha:''' Vache... It's been so many years. Are you still alone in the blizzard...?
:'''Natasha:''' ...Ignore me... I'm just talking to myself. Let's go, (Trailblazer). It's time to face my past head-on.
----
